\h Yohan
\toc1 Yohan (John)
\toc2 Yohan
\toc3 Jhn
\mt2 The account of Yeshua's ministry by
\mt1 Yohan (John)
\is1 Introduction
\is2 Author
\ip This account about the works and teachings of Yeshua (Jesus) was written by Yohan (John), brother of Yacob (mistakenly known in older English Bibles as James). Both of them were in the small group of twelve close followers of Yeshua that he selected as his apprentices and who accompanied him around as he taught. Out of the twelve, Yohan was the one that greatly loved Yeshua, and his closeness gave him much of the insight that he includes with his description of Yeshua's actions and teaching. The two brothers were the sons of Zebedee, and all three of them worked as fishermen on Lake Galilee.
\is2 This account
\ip The \em Open English Translation\em* places Yohan's account before the others because it begins with the eternal existence of Yeshua the messiah. Not only is Yeshua the godly messenger, he was also the creator who has now descended from heaven as a man. Omitting any mention of the baby Yeshua, Yohan does however tell us about Yohan-the-immerser who came before Yeshua to prepare the people for the arrival of the promised messiah.
\ip In chapters two to twelve it's written how the various miracles that Yeshua did showed that he was the promised messiah who would offer life without ending to anyone who would accept that he had been sent by God and trust in his teaching. Although there were indeed many who did believe in him, many others were unable to come to that point and ended up opposing Yeshua at every turn.
\ip In chapters thirteen to seventeen, Yeshua's compassion towards his followers is described. He also told them in advance of his impending brutal death.
\ip In the final few chapters, we read about Yeshua's arrest and trial, then his being fastened to a pole and giving up his spirit, his coming back to life, and how his followers saw him and spoke with him again during that period.
\ip Yohan is careful to explain how to receive life without ending by means of believing that Yeshua came down from heaven and obeying his teaching. Yeshua himself is the path and the truth and the life (14:6).
\iot Main components of Yohan's account
\io1 Introduction \ior 1:1-18\ior*
\io1 Yohan-the-immerser and the first followers of Yeshua \ior 1:19-51\ior*
\io1 The people monitor Yeshua's teaching and miracles \ior 2:1–12:50\ior*
\io1 Yeshua's final week in and around Yerushalem \ior 13:1–19:42\ior*
\io1 Yeshua comes back to life and meets people again \ior 20:1-31\ior*
\io1 Yeshua reveals himself to his followers in Galilee \ior 21:1-25\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\s1 The arrival of the true light
\rem /s1 The Word Became Flesh; The Word of Life; The coming of Christ; Christ, the Eternal Word
\p
\v 1 In the beginning¦62339 was the message,\f + \fr 1:1 \ft TD: This passage is complex to translate because the message was also the messenger—that is, Yeshua came not only to teach about getting saved, but also to become the actual pathway to be saved!\f* and the message was with¦62347 God, and the message was \add and is\add* God.
\v 2 He, \add the message\add*, was with \nd God¦62362\nd* \add even\add* at the creation¦62359 \add of the universe\add*.
\v 3 Everything came into existence through¦62364 \add @the¦62365 messenger\add*\f + \fr 1:3 \ft Lit. him.\f*—\add ≈there's not¦62372 even¦62372 one¦62373 thing that came into existence that wasn't made by\add* him.
\v 4 He holds life, and¦62382 that life is the¦62386 light¦62387 of¦62389 humankind.
\v 5 And that light¦62392 is¦62396 shining¦62396 in¦62393 the¦62394 darkness, and¦62390 darkness cannot overcome him.
\p
\v 6 A man¦62404 arrived who had¦62405 been¦62405 sent¦62405 by \nd God¦62409\nd*. His name¦62412 was¦62413 Yohan¦62414.\x + \xo 1:6: \xt Mat 3:1; Mrk 1:4; Luk 3:1-2.\x*
\v 7 He¦62422 came¦62417 as a testimony¦62420 to tell about¦62423 the light so that¦62426 everyone would believe¦62428 the light.
\v 8 Yohan himself wasn't¦62433 the light—he was merely the announcer of the light.
\v 9 The true¦62447 light¦62445 which¦62448 enlightens¦62449 every¦62450 person¦62451 was coming¦62452 into¦62453 the¦62454 world¦62455.
\p
\v 10 He was¦62459 in¦62456 the world and he's the creator of the world, and yet the world didn't¦62472 even know¦62473 him¦62471.
\v 11 He came¦62477 to¦62474 his own chosen people, but¦62478 they wouldn't accept him¦62481,
\v 12 however anyone who would accept him¦62487 and trusted in his¦62501 authority, he¦62488 gave¦62488 them¦62490 the¦62492 right¦62492 to become¦62495 children¦62493 of¦62501 \nd God¦62494\nd*—
\v 13 not physical children and not coming from human actions, but¦62514 children of \nd God¦62516\nd*.
\p
\v 14 And the message¦62521 became¦62523 a human and lived here among¦62526 us¦62527 and we¦62529 saw¦62529 his¦62532 greatness—the greatness of an¦62535 only¦62535 child of the father¦62537—full¦62538 of grace¦62540 and truth¦62542.
\p
\v 15 Yohan explained about¦62545 him¦62546 and¦62547 loudly told everyone, “\add ≈He's¦62548\add* the one I meant when I said¦62554, ‘There's someone coming¦62560 after¦62558 me, yet who came¦62560 before me, because¦62565 he¦62568 existed before I did!’ ”
\p
\v 16 Because¦62569 he has so much, we¦62575 all¦62576 received¦62578 grace and¦62579 then even more grace.
\v 17 The¦62584 commands came to us through Mosheh¦62587, but¦62593 grace¦62592 and¦62593 truth¦62595 came to us through \nd Yeshua¦62597\nd* the \nd messiah¦62598\nd*.
\v 18 No one has¦62602 ever¦62603 actually seen¦62602 God, but the human son born from God the father¦62617 and in¦62613 close touch with him, he was the one to explain¦62619 God to us.
\s1 The interrogation of Yohan-the-immerser
\rem /s1 John the Baptist's Message; The Testimony of John the Baptist; John the Baptist Denies Being the Christ; Testimony of the Baptist and the first disciples
\r (Mat. 3:1-12; Mark 1:1-8; Luke 3:1-18)
\p
\v 19 Yohan¦62627 explained some of this when¦62628 the¦62633 Jewish leaders sent¦62629 out¦62629 priests¦62637 and¦62638 temple workers from¦62635 Yerushalem¦62636 to ask¦62643 him¦62646, “Who are¦62650 you¦62648?”
\p
\v 20 He didn't¦62654 flinch from the truth and¦62651 so he told them, “I am¦62661 not¦62660 the \nd chosen¦62664 messiah¦62664\nd*.”
\p
\v 21 So¦62665 they¦62667 asked¦62667 him¦62668 again, “Are you¦62674 Eliyah¦62677 come back to life?”\x + \xo 1:21: a \xt Mal 4:5; \xo b \xt Deu 18:15,18.\x*
\p And he¦62681 answered¦62691, “No, I'm not¦62682.”
\p They¦62667 asked, “Are you the¦62686 prophet¦62687?”
\p Again he answered, “No, I'm not.”
\p
\v 22 So¦62694 they¦62693 asked him¦62695, “Who¦62697 are¦62698 you then? We¦62701 need to give¦62701 an¦62700 answer¦62700 to the¦62702 ones who sent¦62703 us¦62704. How do you describe yourself¦62709?”
\p
\v 23 So he said, “I am¦62711 a voice¦62712 shouting¦62713\f + \fr 1:23 \ft We've deliberately omitted putting a comma here, because it's also possible that the comma should go after ‘wilderness’.\f* in¦62714 the wilderness smooth the path¦62719 of \nd Yahweh¦62720\nd*, as¦62726 the prophet¦62730 Yeshayah¦62728 said.”\x + \xo 1:23: \xt Isa 40:3 (LXX).\x*
\p
\v 24 Some of the ones sent¦62733 out¦62733 were¦62734 members of the Pharisee¦62737 party¦62737.
\v 25 These ones asked¦62739 Yohan, “So¦62738 why¦62744 are you immersing¦62746 people then¦62738 if¦62747 you aren't¦62749 the \nd messiah¦62752\nd* or Eliyah¦62755 or the prophet¦62759?”
\p
\v 26 He¦62763 answered¦62760, “I'm¦62765 immersing¦62766 people in water¦62770, but somewhere here among us all¦62773 there's someone you¦62778 don't¦62779 know¦62780—
\v 27 the¦62783 one coming¦62786 after¦62784 me¦62785, and I'm¦62795 not¦62793 even good enough to untie¦62799 his¦62800 sandal¦62805 straps¦62803!”
\p
\v 28 All this happened in¦62809 Beyt-Ania¦62810 \add !(Bethany¦62810)\add* on the east side of the Yordan¦62815 River where¦62817 Yohan¦62820 was¦62818 immersing¦62821 people.
\s1 Yeshua gets publicly revealed
