\v 51 And he¦63301 continued, “\wj Honestly, I'm¦63305 telling all¦63306 of you: you'll be¦63309 seeing¦63309 the sky opened¦63312 up and God's messengers¦63315 going¦63318 up and coming¦63320 down¦63320 on¦63321 me—the son¦63323 of humanity.\wj*”\x + \xo 1:51: \xt Gen 28:12.\x*
\c 2
\s1 The wine miracle
\rem /s1 The Wedding in Cana; The Wedding at Cana; Jesus Changes Water to Wine; Signs and discourses
\p
\v 1 On¦63327 the Tuesday,\f + \fr 2:1 \ft Or possibly, ‘Three days later’.\f* there was a wedding¦63332 in Cana¦63337 in Galilee¦63339, and¦63340 \nd Yeshua's¦63345\nd* mother¦63343 was there
\v 2 and \nd Yeshua¦63351\nd* and his¦63356 apprentices¦63355 were also invited¦63347.
\v 3 When¦63360 the wine ran out at the wedding, his mother¦63376 said¦63374 to¦63380 him¦63381, “They haven't got any more wine.”
\p
\v 4 \nd Yeshua¦63391\nd* answered, “\wj What does that have to do with us, mother? It's not¦63398 the time¦63401 for my¦63402 ministry yet.\wj*”
\p
\v 5 But his¦63406 mother¦63405 told the¦63407 servants¦63408, “Just do whatever¦63409 he¦63414 tells you¦63415.”
\p
\v 6 Now there were¦63417 six¦63423 empty stone¦63421 water¦63422 jars there that are used for¦63431 Jewish purification¦63427 ceremonies. (Each¦63433 one could hold over 70 litres.)
\v 7 So¦63448 \nd Yeshua¦63443\nd* told them to fill the jars with¦63447 water¦63447, and¦63448 they¦63449 filled¦63449 them up.
\v 8 Then¦63453 he¦63454 said¦63454, “\wj Okay, now¦63457 take a sample out and¦63453 give it¦63465 to¦63460 the MC.\wj*” So¦63453 they¦63462 took some
\v 9 and¦63467 when¦63466 the MC tasted¦63468 the water¦63472 that had now turned to wine¦63473, not¦63476 knowing¦63477 where¦63478 it had come from he called¦63489 the groom
\v 10 and exclaimed, “Most people supply the best wine at the beginning \add of the reception\add*, and the cheaper stuff when people are a bit tipsy. But¦63494 you've¦63511 kept¦63513 the best wine until¦63517 last!”
\p
\v 11 This event in¦63529 Cana¦63530, Galilee¦63533, was the first of¦63533 the miracles¦63526 that \nd Yeshua¦63528\nd* did¦63521, and it revealed¦63536 his greatness and his followers¦63546 believed¦63541 that he was from God.
\rem /s1 Jesus Clears the Temple
\p
\v 12 After¦63550 that¦63551, Yeshua and his mother¦63563 and brothers¦63567 and his followers¦63571 travelled east to Capernaum¦63555, but¦63561 they¦63575 only stayed there¦63574 a few days¦63579.\x + \xo 2:12: \xt Mat 4:13.\x*
