\r (Mat. 21:12-13; Mark 11:15-17; Luke 19:45-46)
\p
\v 13 By then¦63580 it was getting close to the time of the Jewish Festival of the Passover¦63585, and¦63588 \nd Yeshua¦63595\nd* went¦63589 down to Yerushalem¦63593.\x + \xo 2:13: \xt Exo 12:1-27.\x*
\v 14 There in¦63599 the¦63600 temple¦63601, he¦63598 discovered merchants selling¦63603 cows¦63605 and sheep¦63608 and doves¦63612, and moneychangers¦63616 sitting¦63617 at their tables.
\v 15 Yeshua formed some cords¦63624 into a whip¦63622 and drove the sheep¦63635 and cows¦63638 out of the temple¦63630 grounds, and he overturned¦63651 the tables¦63649—spilling the coins¦63646 of the moneychangers¦63641 onto the ground.
\v 16 He scolded the ones selling¦63658 doves¦63657, saying¦63659, “\wj Get them out of here! Don't¦63664 be making¦63665 my¦63670 father's¦63669 house into a market.\wj*”
\v 17 That¦63680 reminded¦63675 his¦63679 followers¦63678 of¦63688 the¦63688 scripture: “I'll be¦63691 filled with zeal¦63687 for your¦63690 temple.”\x + \xo 2:17: \xt Psa 69:9.\x*
\p
\v 18 Then the Jewish leaders responded¦63699, “Do a miracle to show¦63703 that you have the authority to do¦63707 these¦63706 things.”
\p
\v 19 But¦63711 \nd Yeshua\nd* answered¦63708, “\wj Well, destroy this¦63717 temple¦63716 and¦63718 I'll¦63722 raise¦63722\wj*\f + \fr 2:19 \ft We couldn't easily use \+em rebuild\+em* here because there's a play on words—see verse 21.\f* \wj it¦63723 again in¦63719 three¦63720 days¦63721.\wj*”\x + \xo 2:19: \xt Mat 26:61; 27:40; Mrk 14:58; 15:29.\x*
\p
\v 20 The leaders smirked, “This temple¦63734 took forty-six¦63728 years¦63731 to build¦63732, and you reckon that you can raise¦63743 it¦63744 again in¦63740 three¦63741 days¦63742?”
\p
\v 21 But Yeshua had been meaning his¦63754 own body¦63753 when he was¦63748 talking¦63748 about¦63749 the¦63750 temple¦63751.
\v 22 In the future when¦63755 he¦63758 was¦63758 actually raised¦63758 from¦63759 the dead¦63760, his¦63764 followers¦63763 remembered¦63761 this¦63767 statement, and they¦63771 believed¦63771 both the \add Hebrew\add* scriptures¦63773 and \nd Yeshua's¦63781\nd* message¦63776.
\s1 Yeshua does miracles and knows thoughts
\rem /s1 Jesus' Knowledge of Human Nature
\p
\v 23 When¦63783 Yeshua was at the Passover¦63790 Feast in Yerushalem¦63787, many¦63794 believed¦63795 in his¦63799 authority because they saw the miracles¦63803 that¦63804 he¦63805 was able to do¦63805.
\v 24 But \nd Yeshua¦63809\nd* never fully entrusted¦63811 himself¦63814 to¦63815 them¦63815, because¦63817 he knew¦63820 what people are like.
\v 25 (He¦63827 didn't need¦63825 anyone¦63829 to tell him what people are like because¦63835 he¦63834 could¦63830 see what any person¦63844 was¦63841 like on the¦63843 inside.)
\c 3
\s1 Yeshua tells Nicodemus about the need to be reborn
\rem /s1 Nicodemus Visits Jesus; Jesus Teaches Nicodemus; Jesus and Nicodemus
\p
\v 1 After dark one evening, a Jewish leader¦63855 named Nicodemus¦63851 who was¦63845 a member of the Pharisee¦63850 party¦63850
\v 2 went¦63860 to Yeshua and¦63867 said¦63868, “Teacher¦63876, we¦63871 know¦63871 that¦63859 God has sent you¦63875 as¦63876 a teacher¦63876, because¦63879 no¦63878 one¦63878 could¦63893 do those¦63881 kinds of miracles¦63883 if¦63891 God wasn't with¦63896 him¦63897.”
\p
\v 3 \nd Yeshua\nd* responded¦63902, “\wj I'll tell¦63906 you¦63908 frankly that no one can \+add get to\+add* see¦63916 God's kingdom¦63918 unless he's¦63915 reborn.\wj*”
\p
\v 4 Nicodemus questioned, “How can an adult be¦63930 reborn? A person¦63928 can't¦63935 just return into¦63937 their mother's¦63941 womb¦63939 and¦63945 then get born¦63947 a second¦63943 time!”
\p
\v 5 But¦63962 \nd Yeshua\nd* continued, “\wj Honestly, I'm¦63953 telling¦63953 you¦63954: unless a person is¦63966 born¦63958 from both water¦63961 \+em and¦63962\+em* the \+nd spirit¦63963\+nd*, they can't¦63956 enter God's kingdom¦63971.\wj*
\v 6 \wj Someone that's born from a body¦63982 is flesh¦63983 \+add and bone\+add*, but¦63985 someone that's born from God's spirit¦63991 is spiritual.\wj*
\v 7 \wj So you shouldn't¦63993 be surprised that I told you that everyone needs to¦64002 be reborn.\wj*
\v 8 \wj The wind blows¦64008 wherever it wants¦64007, and¦64009 you can hear¦64013 its¦64012 sound¦64011 but¦64009 you can't¦64015 actually see where it's coming¦64018 from or where it's going¦64022 to. So too with everyone¦64025 who's born¦64027 from God's spirit.\wj*”
\p
\v 9 Nicodemus replied, “How can all that even happen?”
\p
\v 10 “\wj You're¦64049 a Jewish teacher¦64052,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* answered¦64043, “\wj and yet you¦64058 don't¦64057 know¦64058 all that?\wj*
\v 11 \wj It's true that¦64063 we just teach what we know¦64065, and¦64067 explain what we've¦64065 seen¦64069 ourselves, but¦64067 you¦64077 people aren't¦64076 accepting our¦64074 testimony¦64073.\wj*
\v 12 \wj If I tell¦64090 all of you earthly¦64080 things and¦64084 you don't¦64085 believe them, how¦64088 will¦64086 you ever believe if¦64089 I explain \+em heavenly¦64093\+em* things \+add to you\+add*?\wj*
\v 13 \wj None of you have \+add ever\+add* gone¦64100 up¦64100 into¦64102 heaven, but¦64096 I, the¦64112 son¦64113 of humanity, have come¦64111 down from heaven.\wj*
\p
\v 14 “\wj Just like Mosheh¦64123 lifted up that \+add bronze\+add* snake \+add on a pole\+add* in¦64127 the wilderness¦64129, it's¦64134 \+add also\+add* necessary¦64134 for the son¦64137 of¦64139 humanity to¦64133 be¦64133 lifted up,\wj*\f + \fr 3:14 \ft lifted up / exalted: See https://bibleDifferences.net/2019/04/25/156-exulted\f*\x + \xo 3:14: \xt Num 21:9.\x*
\v 15 \wj so that¦64142 everyone¦64141 who believes¦64143 in¦64145 him¦64147 won't die, but will live forever¦64155.\wj*\f + \fr 3:15 \ft See http://bibleandtech.blogspot.com/2021/03/john-314-21-translation-and-commentary.html\f*
\v 16 \wj Because\wj*\f + \fr 3:16 \ft Sadly when older English translations use ‘For’ (following John Wycliffe's middle-English translation from Latin from the 1300's), it's quite easy to ignore what it's there for. The \+em OET\+em* uses the modern-English translation ‘Because’ which makes the connection to the previous verses (especially v14-15) clearer.\f* \wj in that same way, \+nd God¦64160\+nd* loves¦64158 \+add the people of\+add* the world enough to cause \+add &his\+add* only¦64168 son¦64165 to be born, and to give¦64170 him¦64177 to the world, so¦64163 that everyone¦64172 who believes¦64174 that won't¦64178 die, but¦64181 will \+add go on to\+add* live forever¦64184.\wj*
\p
\v 17 “\wj \+nd God¦64189\+nd* didn't¦64185 send¦64187 his¦64190 son¦64191 here to condemn people, but¦64201 rather to save¦64203 them.\wj*
\v 18 \wj Anyone who trusts in¦64210 me won't¦64212 be condemned. However, anyone who doesn't believe¦64222 this has¦64219 already¦64218 been¦64219 condemned because¦64220 he¦64222 rejected the authority of¦64226 the only¦64227 son¦64228 that \+nd God¦64230\+nd* fathered.\wj*
\v 19 \wj And this¦64231 is¦64233 the verdict: that¦64231 light has¦64239 come¦64239 into¦64240 the world¦64242, but¦64232 some people¦64247 love¦64244 the darkness¦64251 more than¦64253 the light because¦64257 they do evil¦64260 things,\wj*
\v 20 \wj because¦64264 everyone¦64263 who does¦64267 evil¦64266 things hates¦64268 the light and¦64271 doesn't come¦64273 to¦64274 the light so that¦64265 their actions won't¦64272 be¦64279 exposed.\wj*
\v 21 \wj But anyone who does what is¦64292 right¦64291, comes¦64292 toward the¦64294 light¦64295 so that¦64296 their actions can be¦64297 revealed¦64297 as being done with God's help.\wj*”
\s1 Yohan approves of Yeshua's popularity
\rem /s1 Jesus and John the Baptist; John the Baptist Exalts Jesus; John the Baptist's Testimony About Jesus
\p
\v 22 After¦64308 this, \nd Yeshua¦64312\nd* and his¦64320 followers¦64319 went¦64310 down to Yudea, and stayed¦64328 there¦64327 and immersed¦64332 some believers.
\v 23 Yohan¦64337 was also¦64335 immersing¦64338 people at Aenon¦64340 near¦64341 Salim¦64344 because¦64345 there was plenty of water¦64346 there and¦64334 people would come \add to him\add* to get immersed¦64353.
\v 24 (At this point in time, Yohan¦64362 had¦64357 not¦64354 yet¦64354 been¦64357 put in prison¦64360.)\x + \xo 3:24: \xt Mat 14:3; Mrk 6:17; Luk 3:19-20.\x*
\v 25 Then a debate¦64366 about¦64376 purification¦64377 started between Yohan's¦64372 followers¦64370 and a religious leader.\f + \fr 3:25 \ft https://www.billmounce.com/monday-with-mounce/what-does-the-word-%E2%80%9Cjew%E2%80%9D-mean-you-john-3-25\f*
\v 26 So¦64378 some people went¦64380 to Yohan¦64383 and said¦64385, “Teacher, that man that came¦64380 to you across the¦64393 river and that you testified¦64398 about, now \em he's\em* immersing¦64402 people and so they're all¦64404 going to him¦64407.”
\p
\v 27 “None of us get anything if¦64421 it's not being given¦64426 from¦64428 heaven¦64430,” Yohan answered¦64408.
\v 28 “You¦64432 yourselves know that I said¦64436 that I'm¦64441 not¦64439 the \nd messiah¦64443\nd*, but¦64444 rather the one coming before¦64448 him.\x + \xo 3:28: \xt Yhn 1:20.\x*
\v 29 It's the groom that has¦64481 the bride¦64454—the best man is happy because¦64470 he sees that the groom is happy. So¦64476 I'm actually completely happy with¦64468 all this¦64475.
\v 30 It's¦64484 right¦64484 and proper that he should increase¦64485 and I should fade out.”
\rem /s1 He Who Comes from Heaven; The One Who Comes from Heaven
\p
\v 31 “The one who came down from heaven is greater than any of us. We came from this world and¦64507 speak¦64511 in our earthly ways. The one who came down from heaven is greater than any of us.
\v 32 He¦64524 explains about¦64532 what he's¦64528 seen¦64524 and¦64525 heard¦64526, but¦64529 people don't believe him¦64532.
\v 33 Anyone who does believe him¦64537, confirms that¦64543 \nd God¦64545\nd* is¦64547 true¦64546.
\v 34 The one that God sent¦64550 tells us God's words, because¦64559 God doesn't ration his \nd spirit¦64567\nd*.
\v 35 The¦64571 father¦64569 loves¦64570 the¦64578 son¦64572 and¦64573 has¦64575 put him¦64580 in¦64577 charge of¦64580 everything.\x + \xo 3:35: \xt Mat 11:27; Luk 10:22.\x*
\v 36 Anyone who believes¦64583 \add God's\add* son will live forever¦64590, but anyone who disobeys the son won't¦64596 be¦64598 seeing¦64598 life¦64599, but will feel God's severe¦64602 anger¦64602 \add instead\add*.”
\c 4
\s1 Yeshua chats with a woman at the well
\rem /s1 Jesus Talks With a Samaritan Woman; Jesus and the Samaritan Woman; Jesus and the Woman of Samaria
\p
\v 1 When¦64609 \nd Yeshua¦64620\nd* found out that the¦64617 Pharisee¦64618 party¦64618 knew¦64611 that he was gaining and¦64624 immersing¦64625 more¦64621 followers¦64622 than¦64626 Yohan¦64627 had,
\v 2 (although actually it wasn't¦64634 \nd Yeshua¦64630\nd* himself¦64631 that was¦64634 immersing¦64634 them, but¦64635 his¦64638 apprentices¦64637 that were doing it),
\v 3 he¦64639 left¦64639 Yudea¦64641 and¦64643 went¦64644 back¦64645 up to Galilee¦64648.
\v 4 On the way up, he decided to go through¦64653 Shomron¦64655 \add !(Samaria¦64655)\add*.
\p
\v 5 By choosing that route, they came¦64656 to¦64658 a town¦64659 in Shomron¦64661 called¦64662 Sukar¦64663, which¦64667 was near¦64664 the place that the \add patriarch\add* Yosef¦64672 had inherited from his¦64675 father Yacob¦64670,\x + \xo 4:5: \xt Gen 33:19; Josh 24:32.\x*
\v 6 and ‘Yacob's¦64681 well’ was there¦64678. \nd Yeshua¦64684\nd* was tired from¦64686 all the walking and was sitting¦64689 by the well around midday.
\p
\v 7 A woman¦64705 came¦64703 from the town to get water¦64710 from the well, and \nd Yeshua¦64714\nd* asked her¦64712 for a drink¦64717
\v 8 since his¦64721 followers¦64720 had¦64722 gone¦64722 into¦64723 the¦64724 town¦64725 to buy¦64728 some lunch.
\p
\v 9 The woman¦64733 said¦64729 to him¦64731, “You're a Jew. How come you're asking me¦64742 for a drink¦64743 when I'm from Shomron?” (Jews don't¦64751 normally associate¦64753 with anyone from Shomron.)\x + \xo 4:9: \xt Est 4:1-5; Neh 4:1-2.\x*
\p
\v 10 \nd Yeshua\nd* answered¦64757, “\wj If you'd¦64778 recognised God's gift¦64766 and who it is¦64771 who's¦64770 asking you for a drink, you would have asked me and I would have given¦64783 you \+em living¦64787\+em* water¦64786 \+add to drink\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 11 But¦64799 the woman¦64793 \add ≈countered\add*, “Mister¦64794, you don't even have \add rope and\add* a bucket¦64797 to reach the water in the deep¦64803 well¦64801. How then could you get ‘living¦64817 water’?
\v 12 I doubt that you're greater¦64820 than¦64820 our¦64825 ancestor Yacob¦64826 who¦64828 made this well¦64833 for us¦64831 and drank¦64841 this water along with his children and his animals.”
\p
\v 13 \nd Yeshua\nd* \add ≈responded¦64854\add*, “\wj Everyone¦64857 who drinks¦64859 this¦64863 water¦64862 will¦64864 get thirsty¦64864 again¦64865,\wj*
\v 14 \wj but anyone¦64866 who drinks¦64871 the water that I give them will find a well springing up¦64901 inside them—springing into¦64902 eternal¦64904 life¦64903.\wj*”
\p
\v 15 So the woman¦64909 said¦64905, “Okay, then. Give¦64911 me¦64912 some of that water¦64915 so that I won't get thirsty¦64918 and won't have to keep coming out here¦64926 to the well.”
\p
\v 16 Yeshua said¦64928, “\wj First, go¦64933 and get your¦64938 husband¦64937 and then come¦64940 back here.\wj*”
\p
\v 17 “\add Actually,\add* I don't have a husband!” she \add ≈retorted\add*.
\p “\wj True enough—indeed you don't,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦64956\nd* said¦64953.
\v 18 “\wj You've had¦64967 five¦64964 husbands¦64966 and¦64968 you're not¦64972 married to the man you're living with, so what you said was true.\wj*”
\p
\v 19 “Mister¦64985, I can see that¦64987 you're¦64990 a prophet¦64988,” the woman¦64984 \add ≈reacted\add*.
\v 20 “Our¦64993 ancestors¦64992 worshipped on¦64994 this¦64998 mountain¦64997, but¦65000 you¦65001 Jews claim that¦64998 people should only worship there in¦65004 Yerushalem¦65005.”
\p
\v 21 Then \nd Yeshua¦65016\nd* told her¦65014, “\wj You¦65038 need to¦65014 believe¦65018 that¦65032 I was sent from God, woman¦65021, because¦65022 a day is¦65023 coming¦65023 when¦65026 everyone will be¦65038 worshipping¦65038 him neither¦65027 on¦65028 this¦65032 mountain¦65031, nor¦65035 in¦65036 Yerushalem¦65037.\wj*
\v 22 \wj You¦65045 people in Shomron don't¦65044 even know who you¦65045 worship, but we do, because¦65050 people will¦65042 be saved by means of¦65053 us Jews.\wj*
\v 23 \wj But¦65060 a time¦65059 is coming¦65058, starting even now¦65061, when¦65063 the true¦65065 worshippers¦65066 will¦65067 be¦65067 worshipping¦65067 the father¦65069 in¦65070 spirit¦65071 and¦65072 truth¦65073, because¦65075 those are the ones that he is wanting to worship him¦65082.\wj*
\v 24 \wj \+nd God¦65088\+nd* is spirit, and the¦65091 ones worshipping him¦65093 must worship in¦65094 spirit and total honesty.\wj*”
\p
\v 25 The woman¦65105 said¦65102, “I'm aware that¦65108 the¦65109 messiah is coming¦65110—God's chosen one. Whenever¦65114 he appears, he'll¦65117 teach us¦65119 everything.”
\p
\v 26 “\wj \+em I am\+em* the messiah,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦65125\nd* responded. “\wj Yes, he's speaking¦65129 to¦65130 you¦65130!\wj*”
\rem /s1 The Disciples Rejoin Jesus
\p
\v 27 After¦65132 this¦65134, his¦65139 followers¦65138 arrived back, and¦65131 they¦65141 were¦65141 astounded that¦65134 he¦65146 was¦65146 speaking¦65146 with a woman¦65145. However¦65149 no¦65148 one¦65148 dared ask her, “What are you after¦65132?” Or to ask him¦65139, “Why are you talking¦65146 with her?”
\p
\v 28 So¦65162 the woman¦65170 left¦65161 her¦65167 water¦65166 jar there, and¦65171 went¦65172 back into¦65173 the town¦65175 where she¦65177 told the people¦65179,
\v 29 “Come and see¦65181 a man¦65182 who¦65183 knew as much about me as I know myself! He must be the¦65194 \nd messiah¦65195\nd*!”
\v 30 So they¦65203 went¦65197 out from the¦65200 town¦65201 to¦65204 go and¦65202 see Yeshua.
\p
\v 31 Meanwhile¦65210, Yeshua's followers¦65214 encouraged him¦65212, “Teacher, here, eat¦65218.”
\p
\v 32 But he¦65219 said¦65221, “\wj I've had food¦65224 to eat¦65226 that¦65227 you¦65228 don't¦65229 know¦65230 about.\wj*”
\p
\v 33 This made his followers¦65238 ask each other, “Did you see anyone¦65242 bring¦65243 him¦65244 something¦65244 to eat¦65245?”
\p
\v 34 “\wj Obeying God who sent¦65259 me is¦65246 like food¦65251 to me, and¦65261 I plan to finish his¦65263 work¦65265,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦65249\nd* explained.
\v 35 “\wj Don't you all have a saying¦65268 about¦65285 needing to wait four¦65271 months¦65271 for a harvest? But¦65274 I'm¦65279 telling you that you all should open your¦65285 eyes¦65284 and¦65286 look¦65278 at the¦65288 fields¦65289, because¦65290 they're¦65292 already¦65295 lightening up as harvest time approaches.\wj*
\v 36 \wj The harvester gets paid with a harvest that will last forever¦65307 so that the ones who plant and¦65315 the ones who harvest can all celebrate.\wj*
\v 37 \wj There's truth in¦65320 the¦65327 statement¦65325 that¦65332 one person plants and¦65334 a different person harvests.\wj*
\v 38 \wj I've sent¦65339 you¦65341 all¦65341 out¦65339 to¦65342 harvest where you haven't¦65346 worked before—others¦65348 did the groundwork and¦65351 you benefit from their¦65356 work¦65355.\wj*”
\rem /s1 Many Samaritans Believe
\p
\v 39 And many¦65363 people of Shomron¦65368 came out¦65358 of that town¦65361 and¦65359 believed¦65364 that Yeshua is God because¦65369 the woman¦65373 had told¦65376 them that he knew everything about¦65367 her.
\v 40 So¦65390 when¦65382 they all came¦65386, they asked¦65391 him¦65392 to¦65393 stay in their town and¦65398 they stayed on there¦65402 for a couple of days¦65404.
\p
\v 41 As a result of his¦65414 teaching, many¦65407 more¦65408 believed¦65410
\v 42 so then they¦65421 told the woman, “We no¦65425 longer¦65425 believe¦65432 just because¦65426 of what you said¦65421, but¦65417 now that we've¦65436 heard¦65436 him for¦65435 ourselves¦65433, we can see that he really is¦65445 the saviour¦65448 of the world¦65450.”
\s1 Yeshua heals the official's son
\rem /s1 Jesus the giver of life; Jesus Returns to Galilee; Jesus Heals an Official's Son; Jesus Heals the Official's Son
\p
\v 43 After¦65453 his two¦65456 days¦65457 in Shomron \add !(Samaria)\add*, Yeshua continued on up to Galilee¦65464.
\v 44 \nd He¦65468\nd* himself¦65465 had¦65478 told them that¦65470 no prophet¦65471 gets honoured¦65476 in¦65472 his¦65473 own¦65474 home town.\x + \xo 4:44: \xt Mat 13:57; Mrk 6:4; Luk 4:24.\x*
\v 45 When he got to Galilee¦65485, the people accepted him¦65488, having¦65492 seen¦65492 everything that he'd done¦65496 at¦65500 the feast¦65502 in¦65497 Yerushalem¦65499 because¦65505 they¦65504 had also¦65503 been down there.\x + \xo 4:45: \xt Yhn 2:23.\x*
\rem /s1 Jesus Heals an Official's Son
\p
\v 46 So¦65535 he went¦65514 again to¦65521 Cana¦65525 there in Galilee¦65528 where¦65529 he had made¦65530 the¦65532 water¦65533 into wine¦65534. Now there was a royal¦65540 official¦65540 there, whose¦65541 son¦65543 in Capernaum¦65546 was ill.\x + \xo 4:46: \xt Yhn 2:1-11.\x*
\v 47 When the official heard¦65548 that¦65549 \nd Yeshua¦65551\nd* was coming¦65552 up from Yudea¦65556 to Galilee¦65559, he went¦65560 and asked¦65566 him¦65573 if he would come¦65569 and heal¦65572 his¦65573 son¦65575 who was dying¦65578.
\v 48 \nd Yeshua¦65582\nd* said¦65579 to¦65583 him¦65584, “\wj You¦65591 people won't¦65586 believe¦65594 unless you¦65594 see¦65591 miracles¦65587 and¦65588 other marvels.\wj*”
\p
\v 49 But the¦65606 official¦65600 begged him¦65597, “Sir, please come¦65603 before¦65604 my¦65611 child¦65608 dies¦65605.”
\p
\v 50 “\wj Go back there and¦65635 see,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦65615\nd* responded¦65629. “\wj Your¦65619 son¦65618 will recover.\wj*”
\p The man¦65624 believed¦65622 what Yeshua had told him¦65630, and so he¦65636 started off.
\v 51 On his way, his slaves¦65644 met¦65646 him¦65648 and reported¦65651 that¦65655 the¦65656 boy¦65658 was alive and well.
\p
\v 52 So¦65663 the official asked them¦65670 what time¦65667 it was that he¦65674 got better¦65673, and they¦65676 replied that the fever¦65687 had¦65674 subsided around 1pm.
\v 53 The¦65690 father¦65691 knew¦65688 that that was¦65695 the¦65696 time¦65697 when Yeshua had told him¦65701 that his son¦65706 would recover, and as a result his whole¦65716 household¦65714 believed¦65710 \add that Yeshua came from God\add*.
\p
\v 54 This¦65717 was the second¦65722 miracle that¦65717 \nd Yeshua¦65727\nd* have¦65728 done¦65724 after leaving Yudea¦65731 and¦65719 going to Galilee¦65734.
\c 5
\s1 Yeshua heals a man at the pool
\rem /s1 The Healing at the Pool; Jesus Heals on the Sabbath; Jesus Heals a Lame Man
\p
\v 1 After¦65735 all this, there¦65737 was¦65737 another Jewish feast¦65739, so \nd Yeshua¦65745\nd* went¦65743 down to¦65746 Yerushalem¦65747.
\v 2 In¦65750 Yerushalem¦65752 at¦65754 the Sheep¦65756 Gate¦65756, there's¦65748 the Bethsaida¦65766 pool¦65757 that¦65758 has¦65770 five¦65768 alcoves
\v 3 and a large number of¦65778 sick, blind¦65780, lame¦65781, and paralysed¦65782 people¦65776 lie¦65774 there in them.
\v 4 ◘
\v 5 One man¦65825 had been there¦65826 for thirty-eight¦65829 years¦65832,
\v 6 and when \nd Yeshua¦65842\nd* noticed him¦65855 and knew¦65846 that¦65838 he'd been there for so long, he asked, “\wj Do you want¦65856 to get better?\wj*”
\p
\v 7 “Yes mister,” the sick man answered¦65864, “but¦65889 when the water¦65878 starts moving, I don't¦65872 have¦65873 a companion to lift me into¦65883 the pool¦65885, so someone else always get there before¦65893 me.”
\p
\v 8 Then \nd Yeshua¦65900\nd* said¦65897, “\wj Stand up and pick up your¦65907 bedroll and start walking¦65909.\wj*”
\v 9 The¦65915 man¦65916 immediately¦65911 stood up, picked up his¦65925 gear, and¦65910 started to walk¦65927.
\p However, this was the weekly rest¦65931 day¦65935.
\v 10 So¦65937 the religious leaders said¦65936 to the man, “Hey! It's¦65944 against the law for¦65948 you¦65948 to carry your¦65953 bedding¦65952 on the rest¦65943 day¦65943!”\x + \xo 5:10: \xt Neh 13:19; Jer 17:21.\x*
\p
\v 11 But¦65974 the man answered¦65957, “The man who made¦65961 me better told me to pick up¦65967 my bedroll and¦65974 start walking¦65975.”
\p
\v 12 “Oh. Who was it that told you¦65986 to¦65986 take that stuff and¦65992 start walking¦65993?”
\p
\v 13 But the¦65995 man who had been healed¦65997 didn't¦65999 even know¦66000 who it was, because \nd Yeshua¦66007\nd* had quickly left when a crowd¦66010 had formed.
\p
\v 14 Later on, \nd Yeshua¦66022\nd* found¦66018 the man in¦66025 the temple¦66027 and¦66028 told him¦66031, “\wj Look¦66032, you're better now so don't go on sinning¦66036, because you don't want anything worse¦66039 to happen to you.\wj*”
\p
\v 15 The man¦66049 then went¦66045 and¦66050 told the leaders that it was \nd Yeshua¦66061\nd* who had¦66064 made¦66064 him¦66066 better.
\rem /s1 Life Through the Son; Jesus Claims to Be the Son of God
\v 16 As a result, the leaders started harassing \nd Yeshua¦66078\nd* because¦66084 he¦66086 had done¦66086 this on¦66088 a rest¦66090 day¦66090.
\v 17 But¦66104 Yeshua just replied, “\wj My¦66100 father¦66099 is¦66103 working today, and¦66104 so I'm¦66104 also working.\wj*”
\p
\v 18 Because¦66106 of this¦66107, the leaders became determined that¦66107 he must be put to death—not just because he broke¦66121 the rules for the rest¦66123 day¦66123, but¦66124 most of all because he was¦66128 calling¦66128 God his own¦66127 father¦66126, thus making¦66134 himself¦66133 equal¦66132 to God!
\s1 Authority over life is given to the son
\rem /s1 The Authority of the Son
\p
\v 19 So¦66139 \nd Yeshua¦66141\nd* responded to them¦66146, “\wj I want to tell¦66144 you¦66153 all¦66153 something: The son¦66157 can't¦66154 initiate anything¦66173 by himself¦66164. He can only do what¦66180 he sees¦66174 his father doing, because¦66181 whatever¦66180 his father is doing, he also does things like that.\wj*
\v 20 \wj You see, the father¦66197 loves¦66199 his son¦66201 and¦66202 shows him everything that he's doing¦66209. In fact, he'll¦66215 be showing¦66215 him even greater¦66212 things than what he's done already, so that you¦66221 all¦66221 will be amazed¦66222.\wj*
\v 21 \wj Because¦66227 the father¦66229 brings the dead¦66234 back to life, giving¦66238 them new life, so¦66239 too the son¦66242 can give life to anyone who he wants.\wj*
\v 22 \wj The father¦66250 won't¦66246 be judging¦66251 anyone¦66252, but¦66253 has¦66257 already given¦66257 that task to¦66259 the¦66259 son,\wj*
\v 23 \wj so that¦66261 the people might honour the son like they¦66267 honour the father. But anyone who is not¦66271 honouring¦66272 the son, is also dishonouring the father who sent¦66280 him¦66281.\wj*
\p
\v 24 “\wj I assure you¦66285 that anyone who hears¦66291 my¦66290 message¦66289 and believes¦66293 that I was sent¦66295 by God, will live forever¦66299 and will not¦66303 be condemned, but¦66292 has¦66308 moved from death¦66311 into life.\wj*
\v 25 \wj I can also assure you¦66318 that a time¦66321 is coming¦66320, and in fact is here already, when¦66325 the dead¦66327 will be¦66330 hearing¦66330 the voice of¦66333 God's son¦66334 and that voice will bring them back to life.\wj*
\v 26 \wj As¦66342 the father¦66346 is¦66349 the source of life, he¦66359 gave¦66359 the power of giving life to¦66357 the son\wj*
\v 27 \wj and¦66365 gave¦66369 him¦66370 the authority¦66367 to be¦66374 the final judge¦66372, because¦66375 he¦66378 is¦66378 the son¦66376 of¦66377 humanity.\wj*
\v 28 \wj Don't¦66379 be surprised at¦66381 this¦66381, because¦66382 a time¦66384 is¦66383 coming¦66383 when everyone in their graves will¦66398 be hearing¦66398 his¦66401 voice¦66400,\wj*
\v 29 \wj and the ones having done what is good¦66408 will be given new life¦66412, and the ones having done what is evil¦66417 will be condemned.\wj*”\x + \xo 5:29: \xt Dan 12:2.\x*
\s1 The unbelief of the religious leaders
\rem /s1 Witnesses to Jesus
\p
\v 30 Yeshua continued explaining to¦66427 the religious leaders, “\wj I don't¦66423 do anything in isolation. Whenever I hear¦66436 from him, only then do I judge¦66437 and my judgement¦66440 is¦66444 correct and impartial because¦66445 I'm¦66426 not¦66446 imposing \+em my\+em* desires, but¦66438 the desire of¦66456 the one who sent¦66457 me.\wj*
\rem /s1 Testimonies About Jesus; Witnesses to Jesus
\p
\v 31 “\wj If I just testified¦66462 about¦66463 myself¦66464, my¦66467 testimony¦66466 would not be correct or even valid.\wj*
\v 32 \wj However it's another one that's testifying¦66474 about me, and¦66477 I know¦66478 that his testimony¦66484 about me is¦66482 true.\wj*
\v 33 \wj You sent¦66491 people out¦66491 to question Yohan¦66493 and¦66494 his testimony¦66495 was true.\wj*\x + \xo 5:33: \xt Yhn 1:19-27; 3:27-30.\x*
\v 34 \wj but¦66508 I don't¦66500 even need any testimony¦66506 that¦66511 comes from¦66501 people, because I am¦66510 teaching you¦66512 how to be¦66513 saved¦66513.\wj*
\v 35 \wj Yohan was¦66515 a bright and shining¦66521 light¦66531 and you¦66522 appreciated it for¦66526 a short time¦66527.\wj*
\v 36 \wj But I have a stronger testimony¦66537 than¦66539 Yohan's¦66542 because¦66544 the father has¦66547 entrusted works¦66559 to me to complete¦66554, and which I'm¦66533 already doing¦66562 and which clearly show that¦66560 the father sent¦66571 me here.\wj*
\v 37 \wj And since he sent¦66575 me, he himself has¦66581 testified¦66581 about¦66582 me. You people have never listened to his¦66586 voice¦66585, nor¦66591 have you¦66594 ever seen¦66594 him!\wj*\x + \xo 5:37: \xt Mat 3:17; Mrk 1:11; Luk 3:22.\x*
\v 38 \wj And his¦66598 way of thinking is obviously not in your minds, because¦66605 you don't¦66599 believe¦66613 the one that¦66610 he¦66607 sent¦66607.\wj*
\v 39 \wj You look in the¦66615 Jewish scriptures because¦66617 you suppose¦66619 that they'll lead you to¦66625 eternal¦66624 life¦66623. Those¦66629 very scriptures testify¦66633 about¦66634 me¦66635 coming,\wj*
\v 40 \wj yet you¦66638 refuse to come¦66639 to me¦66641 in¦66642 order¦66642 to receive life¦66643.\wj*
\p
\v 41 “\wj I'm¦66651 not¦66650 getting any praise from¦66647 people¦66648\wj*
\v 42 \wj but¦66652 I do know¦66653 that¦66655 you people don't¦66662 actually love¦66659 \+nd God¦66661\+nd* in¦66665 your hearts.\wj*
\v 43 \wj I have¦66669 come¦66669 with my¦66675 father's¦66674 authority and¦66676 you don't¦66677 accept me¦66679, but¦66676 if¦66680 someone came claiming their own¦66687 authority, you'd happily accept them.\wj*
\v 44 \wj How \+em could\+em* you possibly believe¦66693 when you just accept acclamations from each other, but¦66699 don't¦66707 even seek¦66708 praise from the¦66704 only¦66705 \+nd God¦66706\+nd*.\wj*
\v 45 \wj But don't be assuming that I'll¦66713 be accusing¦66723 you¦66715 all¦66715 in front¦66718 of the father¦66720. No, the one who'll accuse you is Mosheh¦66728 because he's the one that you're hoping to please.\wj*
\v 46 \wj The trouble is that if¦66733 you actually believed what Mosheh wrote¦66745, you would believe me, because¦66741 Mosheh was writing about¦66740 me.\wj*
\v 47 \wj But since you don't¦66752 really believe his writings¦66751, you're not¦66752 at all¦66759 likely to believe me.\wj*”
\c 6
\s1 Feeding 5,000 families
\rem /s1 Jesus Feeds Five Thousand; Jesus Feeds the Five Thousand; Feeding the Five Thousand; Bread from heaven
\r (Mat. 14:13-21; Mark 6:30-44; Luke 9:10-17)
\p
\v 1 After¦66762 all this, \nd Yeshua¦66766\nd* crossed the lake¦66769 \add in a boat\add*.\f + \fr 6:1 \ft Here Yohan also uses the Roman name “Lake Tiberias” rather than just “Lake Galilee”.\f*
\v 2 A large¦66782 crowd¦66781 followed¦66778 him¦66780 because¦66784 they'd seen his miraculous healings of sick people.
\v 3 \nd Yeshua¦66807\nd* climbed a hill¦66805 and¦66808 sat¦66811 there¦66809 with¦66813 his¦66816 apprentices¦66815.
\v 4 At that time, it was¦66817 getting close to the¦66824 Jewish Festival of¦66826 Passover¦66823.
\v 5 When \nd Yeshua¦66835\nd* looked out and¦66836 saw¦66837 the¦66834 large¦66839 crowd coming¦66842, he¦66845 asked Philip¦66848, “\wj Where can we¦66850 get enough food from to feed all this crowd?\wj*”
\v 6 But¦66860 he was only saying¦66861 this¦66858 to test¦66862 Philip because¦66866 he already knew¦66867 what¦66868 he was going¦66869 to do¦66870.
\p
