\v 19 When they had¦67126 rowed¦67126 about¦67130 five¦67135 kilometres, they saw \nd Yeshua¦67140\nd* walking¦67141 on¦67142 top of the lake¦67145 and approaching the boat¦67150, and they were¦67153 very scared.
\v 20 But he¦67154 told them¦67158, “\wj Don't¦67161 worry—it's me.\wj*”
\v 21 After that¦67186 they¦67164 were¦67164 willing¦67164 to¦67166 let him¦67167 into¦67170 the boat, and¦67173 immediately¦67174 the boat was at¦67180 their arrival place.
\rem /s1 The Bread from Heaven; Jesus, the Bread of Life; The People Seek Jesus
\p
\v 22 The¦67189 next¦67190 day¦67189, the crowd¦67192 looked across¦67195 the lake¦67197 and saw¦67198 that only one small¦67202 boat had crossed, and they knew that only \nd Yeshua's¦67232\nd* apprentices¦67229 had boarded that boat and left, and not Yeshua himself.
\v 23 Other¦67244 boats¦67251 came¦67249 across from¦67256 Tiberias¦67258 near¦67259 the place¦67262 where¦67263 they¦67265 had eaten¦67265 the bread¦67267 after the \nd master¦67270\nd* had given¦67268 thanks¦67268.
\v 24 So¦67273 when¦67272 all the¦67276 people saw¦67274 that¦67278 Yeshua wasn't around and¦67302 his¦67289 apprentices¦67288 had left, they went¦67303 off looking¦67306 for¦67306 Yeshua in Capernaum¦67305.
\s1 The bread that enables true life
\rem /s1 Jesus the Bread of Life
\p
\v 25 When¦67309 they found¦67311 him¦67312 there across¦67313 the¦67314 lake¦67315, they queried, “Teacher¦67318, how did you¦67323 get here¦67320?”
\p
\v 26 “\wj Honestly, I know that you're not looking¦67334 for¦67334 me because you saw¦67338 \+add God working\+add* miracles¦67339,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦67327\nd* answered¦67324, “\wj but¦67328 because you¦67333 all¦67333 had plenty of food to fill you up.\wj*
\v 27 \wj Don't¦67351 \+add just\+add* work¦67350 for the food which goes off, but¦67357 for the food which lasts forever¦67364—the food which the son¦67367 of humanity will¦67372 give¦67372 to¦67371 you¦67371 because¦67374 \+nd God¦67379\+nd* the father¦67376 has put his mark of approval on him.\wj*”
\p
\v 28 Puzzled, they¦67380 asked him¦67383, “What should we be¦67386 doing¦67386 if we want to work¦67394 for \nd God¦67396\nd*?”
\p
\v 29 He answered, “\wj Doing God's work¦67407 is¦67404 putting your trust in the one that he sent¦67416 here.\wj*”
\p
\v 30 “If so,” they¦67419 said¦67419, “what¦67423 miracle will¦67426 you do for us to see¦67432 so that we can believe¦67434 that you \add came from God\add*? What can \em you\em* do?
\v 31 Our¦67440 ancestors¦67439 ate¦67443 the manna¦67442\f + \fr 6:31 \ft Manna was a word that meant ‘stuff’ and referred to some kind of flakes that regularly came down from the sky in the time of Mosheh and could be eaten as food.\f* out in the wilderness¦67446, just like Mosheh wrote¦67449, ‘He¦67455 gave¦67455 them bread¦67451 from the sky to eat¦67458.’ ”\x + \xo 6:31: \xt Exo 16:4,15; Psa 78:24.\x*
\p
\v 32 \nd Yeshua¦67463\nd* said¦67466 to¦67461 them, “\wj Actually I can tell¦67466 you that it wasn't Mosheh¦67469 who gave¦67470 them bread from heaven, but¦67478 my¦67481 father¦67480 gives you the real bread from heaven,\wj*
\v 33 \wj because¦67493 God's bread¦67494 is¦67498 the one who came¦67500 down¦67500 from heaven¦67503 and¦67504 who gives¦67506 life¦67505 to¦67509 the world¦67510.\wj*”
\p
\v 34 So¦67512 they¦67511 requested, “Mister¦67515, keep giving¦67518 us¦67519 that¦67522 bread¦67521.”
\p
\v 35 “\wj \+em I am\+em* the bread¦67532 that gives life¦67534,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦67528\nd* answered, “\wj anyone who comes¦67536 to me will never hunger¦67541, and¦67544 the one believing¦67546 in¦67547 me, will never be¦67551 thirsty¦67551 again.\wj*
\v 36 \wj But¦67563 as I said¦67556 already, although you have¦67560 seen¦67560 me you refuse to believe¦67565 me.\wj*
\v 37 \wj Everyone¦67567 that¦67568 the¦67571 father¦67572 gives¦67569 to me will¦67575 come to me, and¦67576 I certainly won't¦67582 turn away anyone who comes to me,\wj*
