\v 47 \wj I tell¦67815 you¦67816 sincerely: anyone who believes¦67819 \+add in me\+add* will live forever¦67824.\wj*
\v 48 \wj \+em I am\+em* the bread¦67828 that gives true life¦67830.\wj*
\v 49 \wj Your¦67833 ancestors¦67832 ate¦67834 manna¦67843 in¦67839 the¦67840 wilderness¦67841, but¦67844 they¦67845 all¦67833 went on to die¦67845.\wj*
\v 50 \wj But¦67863 \+em I am\+em* the¦67848 bread¦67849 that¦67850 came¦67855 down¦67855 from heaven¦67853 and¦67863 anyone¦67858 who eats¦67862 this will not¦67865 die¦67866.\wj*
\v 51 \wj \+em I am\+em* the living¦67873 bread that¦67872 came¦67878 down¦67878 from heaven¦67877 and¦67897 if¦67879 anyone¦67881 eats¦67882 this¦67884 bread, he¦67889 will¦67889 live through to¦67891 the next age¦67893.\wj*”
\p
\v 52 At this point, the¦67921 religious leaders began to argue with¦67919 each other, “How could this man give¦67932 us¦67931 his¦67937 flesh¦67935 to eat¦67938?”
\p
\v 53 So¦67940 \nd Yeshua¦67943\nd* explained, “\wj Indeed if¦67949 you don't¦67950 eat¦67952 my flesh¦67954 and¦67959 drink¦67960 my blood¦67964, you aren't¦67950 truly¦67945 alive!\wj*
\v 54 \wj Anyone who eats¦67976 my flesh¦67981 and¦67982 drinks¦67983 my blood¦67987 will gain eternal¦67990 life—I will bring them back to life on that final day¦67999,\wj*
