\v 61 But \nd Yeshua¦68193\nd* already knew¦68185 inside that his¦68204 followers¦68203 were grumbling¦68199 about¦68200 that and asked them¦68207, “\wj Do you¦68210 find that offensive¦68211?\wj*
\v 62 \wj What¦68221 if¦68212 you¦68215 were to see the¦68218 son¦68219 of¦68221 humanity ascending to where¦68224 he¦68225 came from?\wj*
\v 63 \wj It's the spirit¦68247 that is the source of life, not the body¦68234. The concepts that I've¦68243 taught you¦68246 are all¦68246 spiritual¦68247 and¦68249 life-giving.\wj*
\v 64 \wj But¦68277 there¦68253 are¦68253 some¦68258 here who don't¦68261 believe me.\wj*” Actually, \nd Yeshua¦68271\nd* had¦68264 already known¦68264 from¦68267 the beginning¦68268 just who would believe and¦68277 which person would betray him¦68285
\v 65 so he¦68288 said¦68291, “\wj That's¦68293 why I told you¦68292 that¦68290 no¦68294 one¦68294 can come¦68296 to me unless the father¦68307 has given¦68303 them to me.\wj*”
\p
\v 66 After this¦68310, many¦68312 of his¦68317 followers¦68316 went¦68318 back¦68321 and¦68322 no¦68323 longer¦68323 accompanied him¦68325 around.
\p
\v 67 So¦68329 \nd Yeshua¦68331\nd* said¦68327 to his twelve¦68333 \add apprentices\add*, “\wj Don't¦68334 you want¦68337 to leave as well?\wj*”
\p
\v 68 “\nd Master¦68346\nd*,” Simon¦68345 answered¦68339, “if we went¦68349, who would we follow then? You're¦68353 the¦68350 \add only\add* one who teaches about¦68351 living forever¦68352.\x + \xo 6:68-69: \xt Mat 16:16; Mrk 8:29; Luk 9:20.\x*
\v 69 We believe¦68356 and¦68357 know¦68358 that¦68360 you¦68361 are¦68362 the¦68365 holy¦68366 son of \nd God¦68369\nd*.”
\p
\v 70 \nd Yeshua¦68375\nd* responded, “\wj Didn't I choose¦68387 all twelve¦68386 of you myself? And¦68389 yet one of you is¦68395 \+add ?≈the\+add* devil¦68394.\wj*”\f + \fr 6:70 \ft The scriptures appear to teach that although there's many ‘demons’, there's only one ‘devil’.\f*
\v 71 (He¦68396 was talking¦68396 about¦68400 Yudas¦68399, Simon¦68400 Iscariot's¦68403 son, because¦68405 he was the¦68398 one¦68412 who would go¦68407 on to¦68410 betray him¦68411.)
\c 7
\s1 Yeshua's sceptical brothers dare him to go public
