\v 8 \wj You¦68564 all¦68564 go¦68565 on down to Yerushalem ahead of me. I'm not going¦68573 to the feast¦68576 yet because¦68578 it's not yet the right time¦68583 for me.\wj*”
\v 9 After saying¦68590 this, Yeshua stayed up in¦68594 Galilee¦68598.
\s1 Yeshua starts teaching about authentic justice
\rem /s1 Jesus at the Festival of Booths; Jesus at the Festival of Shelters; Jesus Teaches Openly at the Temple
\p
\v 10 But after his¦68605 \add half-\add*brothers had left to go down to Yerushalem, Yeshua also¦68610 went—not in¦68620 the public limelight but¦68601 just incognito so to speak.
\v 11 However at the celebrations, the Jewish religious leaders were searching for him¦68626, and¦68630 were asking around where he was.
\p
\v 12 Even among¦68643 the crowds¦68646 there¦68641 was a lot of quiet banter with some saying¦68650 that Yeshua is¦68653 a good¦68652 man and¦68635 others¦68655 complaining that he¦68660 was misleading the people.
\v 13 Either way, no one¦68664 was¦68667 speaking¦68667 out in¦68666 public¦68666 about¦68669 him¦68670, because¦68672 they were afraid of the reaction of the religious leaders.
\rem /s1 Jesus Teaches at the Feast
\p
\v 14 Finally sometime in the middle¦68681 of¦68679 the celebrations, \nd Yeshua¦68685\nd* went¦68682 into¦68686 the temple¦68688 and¦68689 started teaching¦68690 in there.
\v 15 Even the¦68694 Jewish leaders were¦68692 surprised, asking, “How can this¦68698 man know¦68700 so much when he hasn't been trained as a teacher?”
\p
\v 16 \nd Yeshua¦68707\nd* himself responded¦68709, “\wj My¦68711 teaching¦68712 doesn't come from me, but¦68716 from the¦68717 one who sent¦68718 me.\wj*
\v 17 \wj If anyone¦68721 wants¦68722 to¦68726 do God's will, they'll soon figure out whether¦68732 my teaching¦68731 comes from¦68733 God or¦68738 if I'm¦68739 just making it¦68737 up myself¦68741.\wj*
\v 18 \wj Any person who just teaches their own thoughts is just seeking¦68755 their own advancement, but¦68754 anyone who wants to promote the one who sent¦68759 them, this¦68761 is authentic and¦68764 there's no hidden self-interest.\wj*
\v 19 \wj Didn't Mosheh¦68771 write down God's commands for you, yet not a single one¦68778 of¦68779 you obeys them. Why are you wanting to¦68788 execute me?\wj*”
\p
\v 20 “You¦68797 must be demon-possessed¦68794,” said some in the crowd¦68791, “Who¦68796 would be wanting to¦68799 execute you¦68797.”
\p
\v 21 \nd Yeshua\nd* responded¦68805, “\wj I did¦68809 one¦68807 miracle and¦68810 you¦68813 were all amazed¦68813.\wj*
\v 22 \wj Mosheh¦68817 gave¦68818 you the command about¦68814 circumcision¦68823 (even though it actually came from before his time), but¦68835 to obey this, you'll even circumcise¦68823 a baby boy on¦68836 the Rest¦68837 Day¦68828.\wj*\x + \xo 7:22: a \xt Lev 12:3; \xo b \xt Gen 17:10.\x*
\v 23 \wj So if a \+add baby\+add* boy can be circumcised¦68842 on the Rest Day so that¦68848 Mosheh's¦68854 commands aren't¦68849 broken¦68850, they why did you¦68857 get angry¦68857 with¦68856 me¦68856 because¦68858 I made¦68863 a man¦68860 healthy¦68862 on the Rest Day?\wj*\x + \xo 7:23: \xt Yhn 5:9.\x*
\v 24 \wj Don't¦68866 just ‘judge’ things so that you yourselves look good, but¦68871 judge impartially, seeking the¦68872 best for others.\wj*”
\s1 Could Yeshua be the messiah?
\rem /s1 Is Jesus the Christ?; Is This the Christ?; Is He the Messiah?; Is Jesus the Messiah?
\p
\v 25 After this, some¦68879 of the locals from¦68882 Yerushalem¦68882 started asking, “Isn't this the man they¦68887 were wanting to¦68888 execute?
\v 26 Well, here he is teaching in¦68891 public¦68891, yet they're not even confronting him¦68895. Perhaps¦68899 the leaders¦68904 know¦68901 that¦68907 he really is the \nd messiah¦68911\nd*?
\v 27 But we¦68914 even know where this man is from¦68934. Surely when the¦68917 \nd messiah¦68920\nd* comes¦68929, no¦68931 one¦68931 would know his family background.”
\p
\v 28 So¦68938 as \nd Yeshua¦68948\nd* continued teaching¦68946, he called out¦68936, “\wj Indeed you¦68955 all¦68955 know me and my home and my family. But¦68950 I didn't¦68963 come¦68964 here of¦68961 my own accord, but¦68950 the¦68969 one who sent¦68970 me here is¦68966 truthful, even though you don't¦68963 even know him.\wj*
\v 29 \wj I know¦68978 him, because¦68980 I came from¦68981 him, indeed, he was the one who sent¦68987 me¦68986 here.\wj*”
\p
\v 30 So¦68992 now they¦68991 really want to¦68994 arrest¦68994 him, but¦68995 no¦68996 one¦68996 touched him because¦69006 it was not¦69008 yet¦69008 the¦69010 proper time¦69011.
\v 31 Many¦69022 in¦69024 the crowd¦69020 did¦69041 believe¦69023 that¦69039 he was from God and¦69026 they¦69027 were¦69027 saying¦69027, “When the \nd messiah¦69030\nd* comes¦69032, would he be¦69038 doing¦69038 greater miracles¦69036 than¦69036 what we've seen this¦69040 man¦69040 do?”
\s1 Yeshua discusses leaving as they aim to arrest him
