\p
\v 32 The¦69045 Pharisee¦69046 party¦69046 heard¦69043 the crowd¦69048 muttering about¦69051 these¦69053 things and sent¦69055 out¦69055 some of their servants along with the chief¦69059 priests¦69059 to go and arrest¦69067 Yeshua¦69063.
\v 33 So¦69070 \nd Yeshua¦69074\nd* said¦69069, “\wj I'll only be with¦69079 you¦69080 all¦69080 for a short while longer and¦69082 then I'll be going¦69083 to¦69084 the¦69085 one who sent¦69086 me.\wj*
\v 34 \wj You'll look for me but¦69091 won't¦69092 be able¦69101 to find¦69093 me, and you can't¦69092 go where¦69096 I'll be going.\wj*”
\p
\v 35 The¦69106 leaders wondered, “Where¦69110 could he be going that¦69111 we¦69116 wouldn't be able to find¦69118 him¦69119? Will he go and live with the Jews living out there among the Greeks and start teaching¦69130 the Greeks?
\v 36 And what does he mean about looking¦69145 for¦69145 him and not being able to find¦69149 him, and not being able to go where¦69152 he goes?”
