\p
\v 37 On the final climax day¦69163 of¦69170 the celebrations, \nd Yeshua¦69174\nd* stood¦69172 there and shouted, “\wj Anyone¦69181 who's thirsty¦69182, come¦69183 here to¦69184 me¦69185 and drink¦69187.\wj*\x + \xo 7:37: \xt Lev 23:36.\x*
\v 38 \wj Anyone¦69196 who trusts me¦69191 will have rivers of living¦69203 water¦69202 flowing¦69201 out from him¦69200 just like the¦69198 scriptures¦69195 say¦69193.\wj*”\x + \xo 7:38: \xt Eze 47:1; Zech 14:8.\x*
\v 39 He¦69206 was talking about¦69208 God's spirit that¦69204 the ones who trust him¦69221 would receive¦69214 in the future—not yet because¦69223 \nd Yeshua¦69233\nd* hadn't been lifted up to heaven yet.
\s1 The people are divided about Yeshua
