\p
\v 40 When some in the crowd¦69242 heard¦69246 his teaching, they¦69254 said¦69254, “He really is¦69258 the \add coming\add* prophet¦69261.”
\v 41 Others¦69262 said¦69264, “He must be the messiah.”
\p But some pointed out¦69276, “The¦69277 messiah won't¦69274 come¦69281 from Galilee¦69278.
\v 42 Don't the¦69284 scriptures¦69285 say¦69286 that he'll be a descendant of King David and¦69293 that he'll come¦69302 from David's¦69292 town of Bethlehem¦69295?”\x + \xo 7:42: \xt 2Sam 7:12; Mic 5:2.\x*
\v 43 And so the¦69314 crowd¦69316 was divided about¦69319 Yeshua.
\v 44 Some¦69321 \add of the Pharisees' servants\add* wanted¦69324 to arrest¦69327 him, but¦69322 decided to leave him alone \add for now\add*.
\s1 The leaders distrust Yeshua and mock his followers
