\p
\v 45 So¦69341 when the servants returned back to¦69344 the chief¦69346 priests¦69346 and the Pharisees¦69348, they were asked, “Why¦69355 haven't you¦69357 brought¦69357 him¦69360?”
\p
\v 46 They answered¦69361, “We've never¦69368 heard anyone speak¦69369 like he does.”
\p
\v 47 “Don't tell us that you've also been taken in by him?” the¦69383 Pharisees¦69384 asked them¦69382.
\v 48 “None of our leaders¦69393 or¦69398 any of us Pharisees¦69401 believe¦69394 that he's from God.
\v 49 But all these people ignorant of the scriptures are¦69414 bewitched.”
\p
\v 50 Now Nicodemus (the¦69421 one¦69428 who had¦69422 previously visited Yeshua) spoke up,\x + \xo 7:50: \xt Yhn 3:1-2.\x*
\v 51 “Since when did our¦69442 rules allow us¦69442 to judge¦69443 a person¦69445 before we've even heard¦69448 them out and¦69453 investigated what¦69456 they're doing¦69457?”
\p
\v 52 “So do you come from¦69467 Galilee as well?” they sneered, “Look in the¦69468 scriptures and¦69474 you'll soon see¦69475 that¦69478 no prophet¦69484 emerges out¦69480 of¦69480 \em Galilee\em*.”
