\p
\v 44 Then \nd Yeshua¦74677\nd* called out¦74681, “\wj Anyone who believes that I came from God is¦74693 not¦74692 \+add just\+add* believing in me, but¦74680 \+add also\+add* believing in the¦74698 one who sent¦74699 me,\wj*
\v 45 \wj and¦74701 anyone who watches me \+add working\+add*, is¦74705 watching the¦74707 one who sent¦74708 me.\wj*
\v 46 \wj I came¦74715 into¦74712 this world¦74714 as¦74711 light¦74711 so that¦74718 anyone who believes¦74719 in me¦74721 won't¦74725 have¦74715 darkness¦74724 residing in them.\wj*
\v 47 \wj I won't¦74738 be judging¦74744 anyone¦74730 who hears¦74733 my¦74731 teaching and¦74737 doesn't obey it, because¦74747 I didn't¦74738 come¦74748 to judge¦74750 the¦74751 world¦74752 but¦74753 rather to save¦74755 it.\wj*
\v 48 \wj Anyone who rejects¦74759 me¦74760 and¦74761 doesn't accept my¦74766 teaching does have¦74767 a judge though—it's the message¦74772 that I spoke¦74774 that will¦74776 judge them at¦74779 the end of time\wj*
\v 49 \wj because I wasn't speaking¦74805 from¦74785 my own thoughts, but¦74803 it was the¦74791 father¦74794 himself¦74795 who sent¦74792 me that told me what to say¦74802 and¦74803 what to teach.\wj*
\v 50 \wj And I'm¦74819 fully aware that¦74808 \+add obeying\+add* his¦74811 commands¦74810 leads to living forever¦74813. Therefore¦74818 whenever I speak¦74820, I just say whatever the¦74825 father¦74826 said¦74823 to me.\wj*”
\c 13
\s1 Yeshua washes the feet of his apprentices
\rem /s1 Jesus Washes the Disciples' Feet; Jesus Washes His Disciples' Feet; Farewell discourses
\p
\v 1 Even before¦74829 the actual feast¦74832 part of¦74833 the Passover¦74834 celebrations, \nd Yeshua¦74837\nd* knew¦74835 that¦74852 his time had come¦74839—the time when he¦74847 would leave this¦74852 world and¦74830 \add return\add* to the father¦74855. He loved¦74856 his followers who¦74860 were¦74860 in¦74861 the world right through to the end¦74865.
\p
\v 2 And now it was getting near time for the dinner and¦74868 the devil¦74874 had¦74876 already¦74875 put¦74876 into¦74877 Yudas¦74883 Iscariot's¦74889 mind¦74879 \add the idea\add* of¦74885 handing Yeshua over¦74881 \add to the authorities\add*.
\v 3 Yeshua knew that the¦74902 father¦74903 had given¦74899 everything to him¦74901, putting it under his¦74905 control, and he knew that he had come¦74913 from¦74911 God and would return to God.
\v 4 So he¦74920 got up from¦74921 the¦74922 dinner \add table\add*, changed out of his¦74926 clothes¦74927, and¦74929 wrapped a linen¦74931 towel¦74931 around himself¦74934.
\v 5 Then he put¦74937 water¦74938 into¦74940 the wash¦74942 bowl and¦74944 started¦74945 washing¦74947 the feet¦74949 of¦74950 his apprentices¦74951, wiping¦74954 them¦74954 dry with¦74955 the linen¦74956 towel¦74956 that¦74957 he was¦74958 wearing wrapped around him.
\v 6 After he'd washed a few, he got to Simon¦74964 Peter¦74965 who asked him¦74969, “\nd Master¦74971\nd*, are you¦74972 going to wash my¦74973 feet¦74976?”
\p
\v 7 “\wj What I'm¦74984 doing¦74985 now¦74990,\wj*” \nd Yeshua\nd* answered¦74977, “\wj you won't¦74988 really understand, but¦74979 in the future you will.\wj*”
\p
\v 8 Peter responded, “Well I'm never ever going to¦75000 let you¦75006 wash¦75006 \em my\em* feet¦75010!”
\p “\wj If I don't¦75004 wash them,\wj*” \nd Yeshua¦75018\nd* answered¦75015, “\wj then you won't¦75004 be included in my \+add group\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 9 “Well, if that's so,” Peter¦75032 said¦75029, “don't¦75035 just wash my feet¦75038 but¦75041 my hands¦75044 and¦75045 my head¦75047 as well.”
\p
\v 10 \nd Yeshua¦75051\nd* responded, “\wj Any person who's already washed¦75053 \+add themselves\+add* only needs to wash¦75067 their feet¦75065 now to be clean. And¦75074 so you're clean, but¦75074 not¦75079 every one of you.\wj*”
\v 11 He¦75081 said¦75089 this¦75088 last bit because¦75087 he¦75089 already knew¦75081 who was going to hand¦75085 him¦75086 over¦75085.
\p
\v 12 So¦75096 when¦75095 he'd finished washing their¦75100 feet¦75099, he got dressed again¦75111 and sat¦75110 down and asked, “\wj Do you know¦75114 what¦75115 I just did¦75116 to¦75117 you¦75114 all¦75114?\wj*\x + \xo 13:12-15: \xt Luk 22:27.\x*
\v 13 \wj You call¦75119 me¦75120 teacher and \+nd master¦75125\+nd*, and so you¦75128 should, because¦75131 I am.\wj*
\v 14 \wj So¦75145 if¦75144 the \+nd master¦75153\+nd* and¦75154 teacher of you¦75148 all¦75148 washed¦75147 your¦75148 feet, then you also¦75159 ought¦75162 to¦75164 wash each other's feet.\wj*
\v 15 \wj I have given¦75170 this to you¦75172 all¦75172 as an¦75168 example¦75168 that¦75173 you can also¦75178 do to others.\wj*
\v 16 \wj I can assure you¦75185 that a slave¦75188 isn't greater than his¦75192 master¦75191, and a missionary isn't greater than the¦75198 \+add king\+add* who sends¦75199 him.\wj*\x + \xo 13:16: \xt Mat 10:24; Luk 6:40; Yhn 15:20.\x*
\v 17 \wj If you can figure all this out and then do¦75207 it, you will¦75205 be¦75207 blessed¦75204 \+add by God\+add*.\wj*
\rem /s1 Jesus Predicts His Betrayal
\p
\v 18 “\wj But¦75220 I'm¦75213 not¦75209 talking¦75213 about¦75210 all¦75211 of¦75212 you¦75212. I know¦75216 each one that I chose¦75219, but¦75220 this that was \+add written\+add* in the¦75223 scriptures¦75224 must be¦75225 fulfilled¦75225,\wj*\x + \xo 13:18: \xt Psa 41:9.\x*
\q1 \wj ‘The¦75230 one sharing food¦75231 with¦75228 me, lifted¦75232 up¦75232 his¦75238 boot against¦75234 me.’\wj*
\m
\v 19 \wj So I'm¦75241 telling¦75241 you now¦75240 before¦75243 it happens so that when it does happen, then you'll all believe¦75247 that I am¦75255 \+add the messiah\+add*.\wj*
\v 20 \wj I can assure you¦75259 all¦75259 that anyone who accepts any person that I might send¦75266, they're accepting me, and¦75271 anyone who accepts me, is¦75275 accepting the¦75277 one who sent¦75278 me.\wj*”\x + \xo 13:20: \xt Mat 10:40; Mrk 9:37; Luk 9:48; 10:16.\x*
\s1 Yeshua indicates who will hand him over
